    "result_text": "The test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication rule in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode` \u2014 the single place where an owner's `customerCode` is computed on save.\n\nThe computed base code is still `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`. I added `deduplicateCustomerCode(String)`, which collects every existing owner's `customerCode`, and:\n- returns the base code unchanged when no existing owner already carries it;\n- otherwise appends `'-<n>'`, scanning from `n = 2` upward and returning the first candidate not already in use \u2014 i.e. the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes the code unique.\n\nI added the needed `java.util.Objects` and `java.util.stream.Collectors` imports and updated the Javadoc to document the collision behavior.\n\nThe build passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`), **BUILD SUCCESS**. The rule can't be forced black-box (telephone uniqueness blocks an identical `telephone + lastName`), so the test asserts the guarantee \u2014 distinct owners get distinct codes \u2014 which continues to hold.",
